Build 048 (diagnostic only): EDEN_TASK_PROBE. About every 30 frames the first emulated task draw of a
submission (alternately one aimed at a shadow-sized depth target and one at the 1440-wide view) has its
distribution arguments and the start of the mesh arena copied to host memory; its triangles are classified
(unused slots, bad index, NaN, behind, off screen, outside the depth range, kept) and logged with the draw's
target, viewport and depth state. Rendering unchanged.

